questions.stem:
During a tournament, a helper counts X marks in the second row of this board:
char[][] b = {{'X', 'O', 'X'}, {'O', 'X', 'O'}};
int n = 0;
for (int c = 0; c < b[1].length; c++) { if (b[1][c] == 'X') n++; }
System.out.println(n);
What integer is printed?

A referee detects a main-diagonal win on a 3x3 board with this test:
if (board[0][0] != EMPTY && board[0][0] == board[1][1] && board[1][1] == _____) { winner = board[0][0]; }
Which expression belongs in the blank?

A minesweeper helper counts live neighbors of corner cell (0, 0) with this loop:
for (int dr = -1; dr <= 1; dr++) { for (int dc = -1; dc <= 1; dc++) { if (b[r + dr][c + dc] == MINE) n++; } }
It crashes immediately. What is the fault?

A puzzle box scores the main diagonal of this tile:
int[][] t = {{2, 9, 4}, {7, 1, 5}, {6, 3, 8}};
int s = t[0][0] + t[1][1] + t[2][2];
System.out.println(s);
What integer is printed?

A puzzle shelf stores uneven rows here:
int[][] levels = {{3, 1}, {8}, {4, 6, 2}};
System.out.println(levels[0].length + levels[2].length);
What integer is printed?

A market totals uneven fruit baskets with this correct scan:
int[][] baskets = {{5, 2}, {9}, {1, 1, 1}, {4, 0}};
int t = 0;
for (int r = 0; r < baskets.length; r++) { for (int c = 0; c < baskets[r].length; c++) { t += baskets[r][c]; } }
System.out.println(t);
What integer is printed?

At the winter trials, an uneven results board crashes inside this maximum hunt:
int[][] g = {{2, 7, 1}, {5}, {9, 4}};
for (int r = 0; r < g.length; r++) { for (int c = 0; c < g[0].length; c++) { if (g[r][c] > m) m = g[r][c]; } }
What is the fault?

A rescue roster sums each uneven team correctly with this fragment:
for (int r = 0; r < g.length; r++) { for (int c = 0; c < _____; c++) { t += g[r][c]; } }
Which bound belongs in the blank?

A field study logs uneven transect counts here:
int[][] plots = {{3, 1}, {8}, {4, 6, 2}, {7}};
A counter increments once per cell. What total does it reach?

A bakery totals the middle display column of this case:
int[][] p = {{2, 9, 4}, {7, 1, 5}, {6, 3, 8}};
int s = 0;
for (int r = 0; r < p.length; r++) { s += p[r][1]; }
System.out.println(s);
What integer is printed?

A climate desk totals rainfall station k across all weeks with this fragment:
int s = 0;
for (int r = 0; r < rain.length; r++) { s += _____; }
Which expression belongs in the blank?

Collected over two weeks from five field stations, a rainfall grid crashes inside this sum:
for (int r = 0; r < grid.length; r++) { for (int c = 0; c < grid[0].length; c++) { total += grid[c][r]; } }
What is the fault?

A grocer finds the largest crate count in column 0 of this stack:
int[][] s = {{5, 8}, {9, 2}, {4, 7}};
int best = s[0][0];
for (int r = 1; r < s.length; r++) { if (s[r][0] > best) best = s[r][0]; }
System.out.println(best);
What integer is printed?

A lab counts strong readings above 50 in column 2 of this sensor grid:
int[][] d = {{41, 62, 55}, {70, 48, 53}, {39, 71, 44}};
int k = 0;
for (int r = 0; r < d.length; r++) { if (d[r][2] > 50) k++; }
System.out.println(k);
What integer is printed?

A ferry assigns two seats on an empty chart:
String[][] seats = new String[2][2];
seats[0][1] = "Ava";
seats[1][0] = "Ben";
int taken = 0;
for (int r = 0; r < seats.length; r++) { for (int c = 0; c < seats[r].length; c++) { if (seats[r][c] != null) taken++; } }
System.out.println(taken);
What integer is printed?

A theater search crashes on a half-filled chart here:
for (int r = 0; r < seats.length; r++) { for (int c = 0; c < seats[r].length; c++) { if (seats[r][c].equals(name)) return true; } }
What is the fault?

A mosaic tool shares one row between two slots, then paints:
int[][] grid = {{1, 2}, {3, 4}};
grid[1] = grid[0];
grid[0][0] = 9;
System.out.println(grid[1][0]);
What integer is printed?

A gallery counts only hung frames on a partly filled wall:
int n = 0;
for (int r = 0; r < wall.length; r++) { for (int c = 0; c < wall[r].length; c++) { if (_____) { n++; } } }
Which test belongs in the blank?
